24 course enrolment records were delivered as one batch and are validated against the numbered rules that follow. No batch breaks more than one rule, and a broken rule is broken once. Judge the batch by the listed rules alone, reading each one literally; anything they do not mention is acceptable.

Each record has these fields: enrol_id (text), transfer_of (text), course (text), weekly_hours (whole number), student (text), amount_due (whole number), tuition (whole number), credits (whole number), module (text), mode (text), invoice_ref (text), list_pos (whole number), grant_id (text), needs_lab (text), materials (whole number), lab_slot (text).

Rules to check:
R1. The reference list `courses` must contain every value of `course`.
R2. The lowest allowed `credits` is 1, the highest is 8.
R3. The allowed span of `weekly_hours` depends on `mode`: 4 to 16 for "part_time", 15 to 40 for "full_time", limits included.
R4. `transfer_of` may be empty; otherwise it holds a `enrol_id` found in one of the records above it.
R5. No two records agree in both `module` and `student`; agreeing in just one of the two is fine.
R6. `lab_slot` may be empty only if `needs_lab` is not "yes".
R7. Within the batch, all values of `enrol_id` differ from one another.
R8. Exactly one of `invoice_ref` and `grant_id` must be filled in: never both, never neither.

