Below are the integrity rules for invoice line records and one batch of 16 records to be checked against them. No batch breaks more than one rule, and a broken rule is broken once. Judge the batch by the listed rules alone, reading each one literally; anything they do not mention is acceptable.

Record fields: line_ref (text), page_line (whole number), contract_no (text), credit_for (text), tax (whole number), currency (text), net (whole number), po_number (text), tax_rate (whole number), disputed (text), dispute_code (text), gross (whole number).

Rules to check:
R1. `credit_for` may be empty; otherwise it holds a `line_ref` found in one of the records above it.
R2. Each `line_ref` appears at most once in the batch; a repeated `line_ref` breaks this rule.
R3. `tax_rate` is never smaller than 0 and never larger than 19.
