Below are the integrity rules for shift entry records and one batch of 10 records to be checked against them. Either every rule holds or exactly one is broken, at one spot. Nothing is a violation unless a listed rule, taken literally, forbids it.

Fields per record: entry_id (text), slot (text), project_code (text), break_min (whole number), role (text), corrects (text), roster (text), worked_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), allowance_code (text), overnight (text), hourly_rate (whole number), row_no (whole number), cover_role (text), cost_centre (text), grade (text), approved_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD).

Integrity rules:
R1. Each `corrects` that is given must match the `entry_id` of a preceding record of the batch.
R2. `break_min` must be a whole number from 15 to 75; 15 and 75 themselves are allowed.
R3. `allowance_code` may be empty only if `overnight` is not "yes".
R4. For a record with `grade` = "senior", `hourly_rate` lies between 20 and 52; for a record with `grade` = "junior", between 13 and 24 (limits included in both cases).
R5. Each record fills in either `cost_centre` or `project_code`, but not both and not neither.
R6. The values of `row_no` are consecutive in batch order: no number is skipped or repeated, wherever the count starts.
R7. `role` is restricted to this list: "loader", "picker", "lead", "cleaner".
R8. No two records agree in both `roster` and `slot`; agreeing in just one of the two is fine.

