A loader validates support ticket records batch by batch; the rules it applies and the next batch (10 records) are shown below. The batch breaks one of the rules at most, and then at a single spot. Only the listed rules are checked and each is read literally: data that looks odd but is covered by no rule does not count.

Record fields: ticket_id (text), onsite_min (whole number), team (text), billed_min (whole number), escalated (text), opened_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), queue_pos (whole number), remote_min (whole number), contact_box (text), account (text), reopens (text), closed_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), plan (text), contact_ext (text), manager (text), case_no (text), response_hours (whole number).

Rules:
R1. `billed_min` is the sum of `remote_min` and `onsite_min`; any other stored value breaks the rule.
R2. If `escalated` equals "yes", an empty `manager` is not allowed.
