A loader validates library loan records batch by batch; the rules it applies and the next batch (10 records) are shown below. No batch breaks more than one rule, and a broken rule is broken once. Judge the batch by the listed rules alone, reading each one literally; anything they do not mention is acceptable.

Each record has these fields: loan_id (text), reserve_code (text), reserved (text), desk (text), deposit (whole number), slip_no (whole number), card (text), kiosk (text), branch (text), member (text), copy (text), item_type (text).

Integrity rules:
R1. The reference list `members` must contain every value of `member`.
R2. Each `loan_id` appears at most once in the batch; a repeated `loan_id` breaks this rule.
R3. A `branch` is valid only if the reference list `branches` holds it and marks it "open".
