24 library loan records were delivered as one batch and are validated against the numbered rules that follow. No batch breaks more than one rule, and a broken rule is broken once. Judge the batch by the listed rules alone, reading each one literally; anything they do not mention is acceptable.

Each record has these fields: loan_id (text), kiosk (text), condition_out (text), renewal_of (text), branch (text), card (text), renewals (whole number), reserved (text), days_late (whole number), fine (whole number), copy (text), reserve_code (text), desk (text), borrowed_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), due_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), daily_fee (whole number).

Integrity rules:
R1. `due_on` falls on the day of `borrowed_on` or on a later day.
R2. Of the two fields `desk` and `kiosk`, one is filled in and the other is empty, in every record.
R3. `renewals` is never smaller than 0 and never larger than 5.
R4. The pair (`copy`, `card`) may occur only once in the batch; either field on its own may repeat.
R5. Each `branch` has to appear in the reference list `branches` with the status "current"; an entry with any other status does not count.
R6. In every record, `days_late` times `daily_fee` gives exactly `fine`.
R7. No value of `condition_out` other than "damaged", "good", "new", "marked" is accepted.

Reference list `branches` with 11 entries, one per line (key: status):
BR-13: expired
BR-20: current
BR-29: current
