16 course enrolment records were delivered as one batch and are validated against the numbered rules that follow. No batch breaks more than one rule, and a broken rule is broken once. Judge the batch by the listed rules alone, reading each one literally; anything they do not mention is acceptable.

Each record has these fields: enrol_id (text), tuition (whole number), tutor (text), level (text), mode (text), weekly_hours (whole number), needs_lab (text), starts_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), amount_due (whole number), invoice_ref (text), grant_id (text), list_pos (whole number), course (text), transfer_of (text), ends_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), materials (whole number), lab_slot (text).

Integrity rules:
R1. `level` must be one of the following: "core", "intro", "seminar".
R2. Each record fills in either `invoice_ref` or `grant_id`, but not both and not neither.
R3. A record whose `needs_lab` is "yes" needs a filled-in `lab_slot`; for other records `lab_slot` is optional.
R4. The values of `list_pos` are consecutive in batch order: no number is skipped or repeated, wherever the count starts.
R5. The reference list `courses` must contain every value of `course`.
R6. The allowed span of `weekly_hours` depends on `mode`: 18 to 45 for "full_time", 5 to 20 for "part_time", limits included.
R7. `tutor` must be a key of the reference list `tutors` whose status there is "active".
R8. No two records of the batch may carry the same `enrol_id`.
R9. No record has a `ends_on` that lies before its `starts_on`; the two may coincide.

Reference list `courses` with 10 entries, one per line (key: status):
CR-257: current
CR-300: current
CR-424: current
CR-489: draft
CR-497: expired
CR-498: expired
CR-600: current
