Below are the integrity rules for sensor reading records and one batch of 10 records to be checked against them. At most one rule is broken, and only in one place. A rule asks for exactly what its sentence says; whatever no listed rule covers is not a violation, however odd it looks.

Record fields: reading_id (text), alarm (text), probe (text), taken_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), frame_no (whole number), valid_samples (whole number), operator (text), alarm_code (text), uploaded_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), all_samples (whole number), cycle (text), script_id (text), void_samples (whole number), recheck_of (text), humidity (whole number).

Rules:
R1. Whenever `alarm` is "yes", `alarm_code` must be filled in.
R2. `all_samples` must equal `valid_samples` plus `void_samples`.
R3. The pair (`probe`, `cycle`) may occur only once in the batch; either field on its own may repeat.
R4. `frame_no` rises by exactly 1 from each record to the next one in the batch; the first record may carry any number.
R5. The lowest allowed `humidity` is 5, the highest is 90.
R6. `recheck_of` may be empty; otherwise it holds a `reading_id` found in one of the records above it.
R7. No record has a `uploaded_on` that lies before its `taken_on`; the two may coincide.

