A loader validates course enrolment records batch by batch; the rules it applies and the next batch (10 records) are shown below. The batch breaks one of the rules at most, and then at a single spot. Only the listed rules are checked and each is read literally: data that looks odd but is covered by no rule does not count.

Record fields: enrol_id (text), lab_slot (text), needs_lab (text), amount_due (whole number), invoice_ref (text), weekly_hours (whole number), materials (whole number), transfer_of (text), tuition (whole number), credits (whole number), student (text), grant_id (text), module (text), mode (text), level (text).

Rules to check:
R1. `credits` must be a whole number from 2 to 10; 2 and 10 themselves are allowed.
R2. If `mode` is "full_time", `weekly_hours` is at least 15 and at most 40; if `mode` is "part_time", at least 4 and at most 16.
R3. `level` must be one of the following: "core", "seminar", "capstone", "intro".
R4. Exactly one of `invoice_ref` and `grant_id` must be filled in: never both, never neither.
R5. In every record, `tuition` and `materials` add up to exactly `amount_due`.
R6. `enrol_id` is the record key: a value may occur only once in the batch.
