A loader validates parcel records batch by batch; the rules it applies and the next batch (16 records) are shown below. At most one rule is broken, and only in one place. A rule asks for exactly what its sentence says; whatever no listed rule covers is not a violation, however odd it looks.

Fields per record: parcel_id (text), forwarded_from (text), signature (text), gross_weight (whole number), door_code (text), piece_weight (whole number), declared_value (whole number), scan_no (whole number), sent_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), locker_id (text), pieces (whole number), bag (text), receiver (text), manifest (text), delivered_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD).

Integrity rules:
R1. Exactly one of `locker_id` and `door_code` must be filled in: never both, never neither.
R2. `gross_weight` is the product of `pieces` and `piece_weight`; any other stored value breaks the rule.
R3. `sent_on` precedes `delivered_on` or equals it.
R4. The lowest allowed `declared_value` is 50, the highest is 500.
R5. Each `forwarded_from` that is given must match the `parcel_id` of a preceding record of the batch.
R6. Whenever `signature` is "yes", `receiver` must be filled in.

