Record fields: ticket_id (text), onsite_min (whole number), team (text), billed_min (whole number), escalated (text), opened_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), queue_pos (whole number), remote_min (whole number), contact_box (text), account (text), reopens (text), closed_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), plan (text), contact_ext (text), manager (text), case_no (text), response_hours (whole number).

Rules:
R1. `billed_min` is the sum of `remote_min` and `onsite_min`; any other stored value breaks the rule.
R2. If `escalated` equals "yes", an empty `manager` is not allowed.
R3. A `team` that is not a key of the reference list `teams` is not allowed.
R4. `response_hours` must be from 1 to 12 when `plan` is "premium" and from 4 to 48 when `plan` is "basic"; the limits are included.
R5. Every record after the first has a `queue_pos` that is one higher than that of the record just before it.
R6. Of the two fields `contact_box` and `contact_ext`, one is filled in and the other is empty, in every record.
R7. `closed_on` falls on the day of `opened_on` or on a later day.
R8. `reopens` may be empty; otherwise it holds a `ticket_id` found in one of the records above it.

