16 parcel records were delivered as one batch and are validated against the numbered rules that follow. The batch breaks one of the rules at most, and then at a single spot. Only the listed rules are checked and each is read literally: data that looks odd but is covered by no rule does not count.

Record fields: parcel_id (text), delivered_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), receiver (text), door_code (text), service (text), scan_no (whole number), pieces (whole number), gross_weight (whole number), length_cm (whole number), locker_id (text), bag (text), piece_weight (whole number), sent_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), manifest (text), signature (text).

Integrity rules:
R1. If `service` is "freight", `length_cm` is at least 30 and at most 200; if `service` is "letter", at least 12 and at most 40.
