Each record has these fields: line_id (text), gift_note (text), ship_mode (text), gift (text), sku (text), placed_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), return_mode (text), quantity (whole number), unit_price (whole number), delivery_zone (text), line_total (whole number), replaces (text), order_no (text), line_no (whole number), pickup_point (text), shipped_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD).

Rules:
R1. No record has a `shipped_on` that lies before its `placed_on`; the two may coincide.
R2. A combination of `sku` and `order_no` that turns up in two records is not allowed, although each of the two fields may repeat by itself.
R3. No two records of the batch may carry the same `line_id`.
R4. Going down the batch, each `line_no` is the `line_no` of the record before it plus 1 (the starting number is free).
R5. In every record, `quantity` times `unit_price` gives exactly `line_total`.
R6. Of the two fields `delivery_zone` and `pickup_point`, one is filled in and the other is empty, in every record.
R7. No value of `ship_mode` other than "freight", "express", "standard" is accepted.

