Below are the integrity rules for support ticket records and one batch of 16 records to be checked against them. At most one rule is broken, and only in one place. A rule asks for exactly what its sentence says; whatever no listed rule covers is not a violation, however odd it looks.

Record fields: ticket_id (text), remote_min (whole number), billed_min (whole number), onsite_min (whole number), severity (whole number), manager (text), escalated (text), product (text), case_no (text), queue_pos (whole number), reopens (text), account (text).

Rules to check:
R1. Every value of `product` must be an entry of the reference list `products` that is marked "approved".
R2. `severity` stays within 1 to 4, limits included.
R3. Every record after the first has a `queue_pos` that is one higher than that of the record just before it.
