A loader validates support ticket records batch by batch; the rules it applies and the next batch (16 records) are shown below. No batch breaks more than one rule, and a broken rule is broken once. Judge the batch by the listed rules alone, reading each one literally; anything they do not mention is acceptable.

Fields per record: ticket_id (text), remote_min (whole number), team (text), reopens (text), closed_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), onsite_min (whole number), billed_min (whole number), escalated (text), case_no (text), product (text), queue_pos (whole number), opened_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), contact_ext (text), channel (text), contact_box (text), account (text), manager (text).

Integrity rules:
R1. The reference list `teams` must contain every value of `team`.
R2. The pair (`account`, `case_no`) may occur only once in the batch; either field on its own may repeat.
R3. `closed_on` falls at least one day after `opened_on`.
R4. Each `reopens` that is given must match the `ticket_id` of a preceding record of the batch.
R5. `product` must be a key of the reference list `products` whose status there is "active".
R6. Whenever `escalated` is "yes", `manager` must be filled in.
R7. `billed_min` must equal `remote_min` plus `onsite_min`.
R8. `channel` is restricted to this list: "walk_in", "phone", "portal".

Reference list `teams` with 12 entries, one per line (key: status):
