24 library loan records were delivered as one batch and are validated against the numbered rules that follow. No batch breaks more than one rule, and a broken rule is broken once. Judge the batch by the listed rules alone, reading each one literally; anything they do not mention is acceptable.

Record fields: loan_id (text), due_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), member (text), card (text), slip_no (whole number), copy (text), reserve_code (text), condition_out (text), reserved (text), borrowed_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), renewals (whole number), renewal_of (text).

Rules to check:
R1. No two records of the batch may carry the same `loan_id`.
R2. `condition_out` must be one of the following: "worn", "good", "marked".
R3. `card` and `copy` together identify a record: two records with the same `card` must differ in `copy`.
R4. `renewals` must be a whole number from 0 to 3; 0 and 3 themselves are allowed.
R5. Every record after the first has a `slip_no` that is one higher than that of the record just before it.
