A loader validates library loan records batch by batch; the rules it applies and the next batch (24 records) are shown below. Either every rule holds or exactly one is broken, at one spot. Nothing is a violation unless a listed rule, taken literally, forbids it.

Record fields: loan_id (text), slip_no (whole number), daily_fee (whole number), fine (whole number), item_type (text), reserve_code (text), desk (text), member (text), days_late (whole number), card (text), renewals (whole number), renewal_of (text), reserved (text), branch (text), copy (text), deposit (whole number), kiosk (text).

Rules to check:
R1. Each record fills in either `kiosk` or `desk`, but not both and not neither.
R2. The reference list `members` must contain every value of `member`.
R3. Each `branch` has to appear in the reference list `branches` with the status "active"; an entry with any other status does not count.
R4. If `reserved` equals "yes", an empty `reserve_code` is not allowed.
R5. The allowed span of `deposit` depends on `item_type`: 2 to 9 for "media", 6 to 30 for "book", limits included.
R6. `renewals` must be a whole number from 0 to 3; 0 and 3 themselves are allowed.
R7. No two records agree in both `copy` and `card`; agreeing in just one of the two is fine.
R8. The stored `fine` has to match `days_late` x `daily_fee`.

Reference list `members` with 15 keys: MB-1186, MB-1889, MB-2905, MB-3900, MB-4668, MB-5608, MB-6349, MB-6594, MB-7286, MB-7889, MB-7926, MB-7948, MB-9266, MB-9318, MB-9381

