An import job checks every batch of parcel records against the integrity rules below before it is loaded; this batch has 24 records. The batch breaks one of the rules at most, and then at a single spot. Only the listed rules are checked and each is read literally: data that looks odd but is covered by no rule does not count.

Fields per record: parcel_id (text), scan_no (whole number), door_code (text), pieces (whole number), manifest (text), locker_id (text), forwarded_from (text), bag (text), service (text), delivered_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), receiver (text), signature (text), piece_weight (whole number), gross_weight (whole number), packaging (text), length_cm (whole number), sent_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD).

Rules to check:
R1. `sent_on` lies strictly before `delivered_on`: the same day breaks the rule.
R2. Within the batch, all values of `parcel_id` differ from one another.
